; FILED: non-integral float `remainder`/`modulo` — NATIVE is the wrong side.
; R7RS restricts both to integers, so results here are implementation-defined,
; but native's are not even self-consistent:
; native -r : -0.5 then 6192449487634432   (the modulo result is garbage)
; vm        : 1.5  then 1.5                 (fmod / floored fmod)
; The zero-divisor cases DO agree after the VM fix: (remainder 1.0 0.0) is
; +nan.0 on both, and (modulo 1.0 0.0) is fatal on both.
(display (remainder 5.5 2.0))
(newline)
(display (modulo 5.5 2.0))
(newline)
